cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Kipp: a hand-written Qwen3 inference engine"
message: "If you use Kipp or its measurements in academic work, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: David
    family-names: "Khachatryan Johansson"
    affiliation: "Polished Snow"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Polished-Snow/Kipp"
url: "https://polished-snow.github.io/Kipp/"
abstract: >-
  Kipp is a small inference engine written by hand in C11 for the pinned Qwen3
  dense checkpoints, with an Apple Metal backend and an isolated NVIDIA CUDA
  backend. Every GPU kernel is gated against a scalar CPU reference on real
  hardware: paged and pooled KV layouts must reproduce the contiguous layout
  bitwise under a deliberately scrambled block table, and GPU logits must match
  the oracle within a documented tolerance with an identical arg max.
keywords:
  - inference engine
  - large language models
  - Qwen3
  - Metal
  - CUDA
  - Apple silicon
  - quantization
  - paged attention
  - speculative decoding
license: MIT
version: 0.0.8
date-released: "2026-08-09"
